    <h2>About Us</h2>
    <p>
      Youth for Cause Foundation is a youth-led initiative created by a group of passionate kids from the Greater Toronto Area. The foundation is dedicated to supporting community workers such as firefighters, police officers, healthcare workers, and waste management professionals, who play a crucial role in keeping our communities safe and running smoothly.
    </p>
    
    <p>
      The foundation's journey began in the autumn of 2022, when a group of young friends decided to organize a simple lemonade stand to raise funds for firefighters battling deadly wildfires in Alberta. This small act of kindness quickly grew into a larger movement, and today, the foundation runs various programs that engage kids in volunteering opportunities across Peel Region. Our future plans include expanding these programs and building a stronger, more supportive community for future generations.
    </p>

    <h3>Our Mission</h3>
    <p>
      To inspire youth to make a positive impact in their communities by volunteering and supporting essential services like firefighters, police, healthcare workers, and more. We believe in a future where every young person feels empowered to contribute to society, making our world a better place for all.
    </p>

    <h3>Our Vision</h3>
    <p>
      We envision a world where youth actively participate in community service, environmental sustainability, and helping those in need. Our aim is to build a culture of care, kindness, and social responsibility that lasts for generations.
    </p>

    <h3>Our Founder</h3>
    <p>
      The foundation is currently led by <strong>Mesha Vaid</strong>, a 9-year-old student at Alloa Public School in Caledon. Mesha's leadership and vision have guided the foundation from its humble beginnings to a growing movement that continues to inspire others to make a difference.
    </p>
    
